, as well as other harmful substances. COPD is often associated with bronchiectasis and can also be related to cystic fibrosis. The condition not only affects respiratory function but can also negatively impact muscle mass and strength, particularly in older adults. Additionally, individuals with COPD may require nutritional support to manage their health effectively.", "RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS:Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition that can contribute to muscle weakness and sarcopenia in older adults.", "FISIOPATOLÓGIA DE LA FRAGILIDAD:La fisiopatología de la fragilidad se refiere a los cambios biológicos y metabólicos que ocurren en el cuerpo, especialmente en los sistemas inmunológico, neuroendocrino y musculoesquelético, que contribuyen a la fragilidad en los ancianos.", "FNT-Α:El factor de necrosis tumoral alfa (FNT-α) es una citoquina involucrada en la inflamación y se ha asociado con la fragilidad y la sarcopenia.", "SISTEMA NEUROENDOCRINO:El sistema neuroendocrino es un sistema que regula las hormonas en el cuerpo y se ha relacionado con la aparición de fragilidad en el envejecimiento.", "SISTEMA MUSCULOESQUELÉTICO:El sistema musculoesquelético incluye músculos y huesos, y su deterioro está asociado con la fragilidad y la sarcopenia en los ancianos.", "FISICA:Física is a field of study that encompasses the principles of matter and energy, often related to health and physical conditions such as sarcopenia and frailty.", "CES-D:The Center for Epidemiologic Studies Depression Scale (CES-D) is a screening tool used to identify depressive symptoms in the general population.", "PATOLOGIAS ESPECIFICAS:Patologías específicas refers to specific health conditions that may be diagnosed based on certain criteria, including frailty.", "INTERVENCION NUTRICIONAL:Intervención nutricional refers to dietary interventions aimed at improving nutritional status, particularly in the elderly to combat frailty and sarcopenia.", "EJERCICIO FISICO:Ejercicio físico refers to physical exercise, which is an important component in the management and prevention of frailty and sarcopenia.", "MUSCULO:Músculo refers to muscle tissue, which has a maximum storage limit for creatine. This tissue is influenced by supplementation, indicating that the amount of creatine that can be stored in muscle is finite and can be enhanced through dietary or supplemental means.", "FRAIL:Frail is a set of criteria used to evaluate the fragility of elderly individuals, focusing on their physical capabilities and health status."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}